{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>What profit</b>. On the pattern of זכרון, and it is a noun from the verbs whose second [root] letter is missing and the hiphil pattern indicates it. The meaning: since all is vanity, what benefit does a person gain from all his labor? The meaning of \"under the sun\" is the revolving time, for the sun alone generates time: the day depends on the sun from the time of its rising until its setting, and the night is from the time of the sun's setting until its rising—whether the stars or the moon are seen or not. Likewise sowing and harvest, cold and heat, summer and winter, according to the sun's inclination toward the north or south side. Although the moon has influence on rivers and moist plants, and in the brain there are fine works—just as the kimah to bind and the kesil to open—their works are none compared to his, but only a portion among many portions. And if the sun is one, its works change according to the change of the six and twenty partnerships of the seven, and the change of all their courses is together with the motion of the height of the solid sphere that goes out. Therefore you will not find the arrangement of the work of the heavens duplicated in another arrangement even for a single moment. And upon this it is mentioned in the Book of Formation: two stones build two, up to nine—which the mouth cannot speak and the ear cannot hear. And the labor to seek wisdom, until my spirit is proven, has profit, for the spirit of man is not under the sun."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The text contains dense astrological/astronomical terminology (e.g. כימה = Pleiades, כסיל = Orion, from Job 38:31); rendered transliterations literally without expansion. גלגל המוצק rendered 'solid sphere' per medieval cosmology. Several phrases are textually compressed or possibly corrupt (e.g. ועשרים מחברות השבעה, עם נוע גובה); translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:02.194606508Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}